3. How sortByKey() works: find the boundaries, then sort
========================================================================
sorted keys: ['02138', '10001', '10001', '30301', '60601', '73301', '94105', '95050', '95050', '95050', '98101', '98101']
boundaries (keys at 1/3 and 2/3): ['60601', '95050']
Keys up to '60601' -> printer 1, up to '95050' -> printer 2, the
rest -> printer 3. All three 95050 statements must stay together,
so printer 3 got only 2: the batches are only ROUGHLY equal.

