========================================================================
6. A common mistake: sorting numbers stored as strings
========================================================================
amounts as strings, 'largest' first: ['99.00', '9.50', '88.00', '75.00', '64.75']
  -> '99.00' first ('9' is the largest first character), and the
     real largest amount '310.25' much later.
amounts as numbers, largest first:   [310.25, 210.4, 150.0, 120.0, 99.0]

int('02138') = 2138  <- only 4 digits: not a valid ZIP code
Rule: sort by the type that has the order you want. Amounts are
numbers; ZIP codes, phone and account numbers are fixed-width strings.
